  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Core state",
      "items": [
        "users carries role/user_type check constraints, is_active/is_blocked/is_verified and the provider id columns the OAuth flows link by",
        "sessions hold the opaque rotating refresh token with ip/ua and an absolute expires_at set at login",
        "codes live in email_verifications (24h) and password_resets (30m, rate-limited per email)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Outbox",
      "items": [
        "the use case writes the state change and the outbox row in one Drizzle transaction — the row is the durability boundary",
        "the worker claims due rows and relays them into BullMQ jobs keyed on the row id; Redis only holds the queue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Delivery + ledgers",
      "items": [
        "failures back off with capped exponential delay and dead-letter into the queue's DLQ, staying visible in the row's last_error",
        "audit_logs records admin actions; the janitor purges expired sessions and code rows on its own loop",
        "the pool is sized for PgBouncer transaction pooling — never for bare Postgres across replicas"
      ]
    }
  ]
}